  "profileMapping": {
    "card": "entity type `node` (attribute `name` = label)",
    "zone": "entity type `container` (attribute `name` = label, unique per scene)",
    "parent": "relation type `contains` (role parent = the zone, role child = the card or zone); hierarchy `containment`, tree",
    "relation": "relation type `link` (role source = from, role target = to, attribute `label`)",
    "extraFields": "detail, tint, code, role, name, footer, store and style are HRPN rendering data outside generic@1 attributes"
  },
  "coordinates": "none: no position, size, route or layout hint; the design system computes the layout",
  "scene": {
    "id": "S2-target",
    "title": "Option 2 decided target · Pub/Sub → Cloud Run single runtime",
    "caption": "Decided target of option B, the target figure of the ARD (owner round r1, 2026-10-19; S2 2026-10-20). D1 = B: one runtime, the Cloud Run backend\nrunning the ADK agent in process. S3 = Pub/Sub: Chat app → events topic → push subscription (OIDC, dedicated push service account) →\n`/gchat-push` → event guard (verification, dedup on the Pub/Sub `message_id`) → consumer, agent run finished before the ack. S1 = RAG Engine.\nColours: blue = GenAiR template kept unchanged; yellow = existing HRPN code kept; orange = new or changed in the target (eligibility before\nretrieval, HR prompt with read-only tools, link formatter for Workspace links (HR05), 1–5 rating as `feedback_score` into the sink and the\nBigQuery linked dataset, PII-scrubbed conversation log kept 1 year (HR04), Model Armor, governed ingestion Drive → GCS → RAG import (HR02));\nno fill = Google or third-party managed service. HR01 = A without ChatUI: no web channel, so no load balancer, IAP or ADK web UI; Agent Engine, admin tools, template bucket and template Firestore `hrpn-datapipelines` are not drawn (removal list: decision dossier §9.7).\nS2 = Firestore (owner, 2026-10-20): ADK's native `FirestoreSessionService` on the Terraform-declared Firestore database `hrpn-sessions` (sessions, history, feedback; TTL policy for the 1-year operational history of HR04); Cloud SQL carries only the Phoenix DB, kept only if Phoenix is kept (owner item, open).\nOpen: gate G1 (publisher exception, VPC-SC), PROD project ids, SCM host, PROD SSM mirror.\nPROD (GenAiR-Cutter PROD mode): `--prod` regeneration with an `app_code`; SCM push → Jenkins on AWS (WIF `iac-sa`) → `develop` / `int` / `main` → dev / int / pro.",
    "legendPassages": [
      "Colours: blue = GenAiR template kept unchanged; yellow = existing HRPN code kept; orange = new or changed in the target (eligibility before retrieval, HR prompt with read-only tools, link formatter for Workspace links (HR05), 1–5 rating as `feedback_score` into the sink and the BigQuery linked dataset, PII-scrubbed conversation log kept 1 year (HR04), Model Armor, governed ingestion Drive → GCS → RAG import (HR02)); no fill = Google or third-party managed service. HR01 = A without ChatUI: no web channel, so no load balancer, IAP or ADK web UI; Agent Engine, admin tools, template bucket and template Firestore `hrpn-datapipelines` are not drawn (removal list: decision dossier §9.7)."
    ]
  },
